      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Grindstone Indian Rancheria of Wintun-Wailaki Indians, founded in 1907, sits about seven miles north of Elk Creek and conducts business there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elk_Creek%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Elk Creek itself is a stream that flows east out of the Coast Range mountains into Stony Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elk_Creek%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Just north of Stony Gorge Reservoir lies the town of Elk Creek, placing it near one of California’s largest reservoirs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elk_Creek%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
